// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'true'
//
// The INVERSE of keyword-as-identifier.pure, and the reason that fixture is not the whole
// story. Domain's identifier rule is extremely permissive -- `Class`, `let`, `all`,
// `toBytes`, `as`, `native`, `projects`, `stereotypes` are every one of them legal
// property names, as the alternatives list in this very message advertises. `true` is not,
// because boolean literals are lexed by a different rule that the identifier arm does not
// include.
//
// So a rewrite cannot get this right with either blanket policy. "Keywords are reserved"
// rejects a property called `Class`; "any word is an identifier" accepts a property called
// `true`. The line is drawn in a specific place and has to be copied, not reasoned out.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::PropertyNamedTrue
{
   true: String[1];
}
